WEBVTT

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:11.330
The Imber has arrived at the
target intercept point.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:16.700
Target speed has increased.
Trajectory error revision: 0.012.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.120
Sending revised data.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.200
Twenty seconds to target area.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.540
Revising Nebula backup point.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.370
Target has entered visual range.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:35.250
Target acquisition in 10.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.870
Target destruction confirmed.

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:56.580
That's a wrap.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.580
Beginning damage evaluation.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.410
Reaction damage: 5.3.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:09.580
Accumulated frame stress
poses no obstacle to return.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:14.250
Fragment trajectory estimates are all green.
They'll burn up in the atmosphere.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.620
Excellent work.

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:19.410
To think, we now have another hand
to destroy the Drops...

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.200
You've shown remarkable growth.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.120
We did it.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:26.120
We did it, Imber!

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:48.790
I've heard the S.O.S.

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:53.700
Have you finally heard it?

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.700
In a cutesy way

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:13.250
Impure or pure, which character?

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:16.080
Maybe they're the same

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.620
The love beat is opened up full throttle

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:23.620
I've noticed, this is a special mission... I've got it

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:30.000
I'll show you for real, because I'll make it come true

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.870
In a world that's pierced through the skies

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:40.830
I felt a strange emotion, I liked you in an instant!

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:45.910
I'm sure I'll win with a smile

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:49.250
Sure enough a smile is the right way

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:54.790
I was small and crying but I'll rise to the challenge

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:57.120
I wonder what this palpitation is

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:00.450
I need a little medical attention

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:08.540
This feeling of slight fever
could be your fault, S.O.S!

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:19.080
A retest...

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:25.410
Cold Hands, Warm Hands

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:20.160
Ma'am?

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:25.250
Yes. In theory for you, Haruka.
And in practice for Yukiho.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.950
You can imagine what I'll be testing, right?

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:29.870
Um...

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.790
The exam will be in two weeks.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:36.000
It will have a major impact on
your progress, so keep that in mind.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:40.660
Um, a major impact? How...?

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:41.870
Oh, that's right.

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:46.290
I'll be sure to pull you both
from your shifts. Do your best.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.450
Ah. Uh...

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:55.750
It's like...

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.450
TEA ROOM
MSSR.
It's way too harsh.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:00.950
I never thought we'd have to do
MORE testing after having come so far.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:02.700
What are you talking about?

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:05.040
You're the one who's bad
for having to take a retest.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:07.200
You brought it on yourself. How shameful!

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.830
Well, this material is too tough!

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:14.950
Reynolds numbers and
Compton effects... I don't get it!

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:18.700
What did you expect? We're Idolmasters!

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:23.370
One error could have grave
consequences for the world.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.950
Does that register in that head of yours?

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.580
Yes, I get it!

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.410
"I did my calculations wrong" or

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:32.500
"I couldn't move when
it counted most" just won't cut it!

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:38.660
Systems are all green.
The Imber is prepped for startup.

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:41.950
Understood.
All right, beginning startup test.

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:44.580
The Imber is starting up.

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:00.450
Yukiho? What is it, Yukiho?

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.450
Um, oh. It's nothing.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:05.500
This is no time to be down on yourself!

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:10.540
We Idolmasters must move forward,
period! Am I wrong?!

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:12.080
I-I get it.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.410
Sorry I'm late!

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.330
Oh, Yayoi!

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:17.750
I'm sorry to ask you to do this.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:21.250
But we aren't getting any postcards
recently. Things are REALLY bad!

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:23.370
As in, if we get any fewer postcards,

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:26.500
our show's getting the axe,
for real, really for real...

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:31.250
I-it's okay, seriously.
After all, I'm a listener. Right?

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:35.660
What do you mean, "Right"?!
Why do I have to do this, too?

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:36.540
I'm NOT a listener-

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:39.790
Thank you! A friend in need
is a friend indeed, right?

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:41.160
Hey, listen to me!

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:42.950
Oh, speaking of...

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:47.830
Once you're done, do THESE, okay?

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.120
Make them out to the "Special Selection:
My Good Luck Charm" segment, please.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:54.620
Oh, also...

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:57.330
Keep your handwriting in mind, 'kay?

00:05:58.700 --> 00:05:59.620
Okay!

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:02.040
Now it's perfect.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:08.500
You'll watch over my studies.
And I'll support your practice drills.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:11.040
We don't have much time,
but let's do our best.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:13.120
Okay. Let's try our best!

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:15.870
Well, should we go ahead and get started?

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:17.700
Huh? Um, tomorrow should be fine...

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:18.750
Haruka!
Huh? Um, tomorrow should be fine...

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:30.080
Good job, Yukiho! That's it!

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:34.580
Just like that. Just like that!

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:48.120
You were so close.
Just a little more would've done it.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:49.330
Yeah...

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:55.330
Times like that, you've gotta go like this,
like that, and like THIS, I think.

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:57.290
Huh?

00:06:57.290 --> 00:07:00.410
I mean, like this. And like THIS!

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:03.000
Um...

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:09.040
Wait! Haruka!

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:12.750
Look, like this. And this.
But here's more like...

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:13.580
Um...

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:15.580
I said, like THIS.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:17.160
What dance is that?

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.200
Like this!

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:23.330
Honestly, I can't bear to watch this.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:28.000
If you want to guide someone,
you need logic and consistency.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:31.200
It wouldn't be hard if people understood
"Like this" or "Like that".

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:34.370
Oh, good work, Coach.
That's an excellent point.

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:36.620
What do you mean, "Coach"?

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:40.580
I just couldn't stand watching
Idiot Ribbon's foolishness anymore!

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:42.410
So you're going to show her how it's done?

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:42.790
Why the heck should I?
So you're going to show her how it's done?

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:44.580
Why the heck should I?

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:47.410
Really? Good thing huh, Yukiho?

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:49.080
Come on, Yukiho, you have to ask her, too.

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:51.040
Now look here!
Come on, Yukiho, you have to ask her, too.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:56.330
Uh, yeah. I-I'd be very grateful. Coach!

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:03.160
Listen up!

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:04.950
Now that I'm your coach,

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:08.160
come senior year, you're gonna
have your eyes on the national prize!

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:09.290
Yes, Coach!

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:09.870
I can't hear you!

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:11.080
"National"?
I can't hear you!

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:11.200
Yes, Coach!

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.660
She sure is a coach.
Yes, Coach!

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:13.040
She sure is a coach.
That's no good. One more time!

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:14.120
That's no good. One more time!

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:15.660
Yes, Coach!

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:23.660
Yukiho has heart, but she's timid.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:27.580
The problem is going to be getting her
to see things to the end.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.160
Yeah.

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:33.620
Maybe going forward, you'll rework
your schedule with that in mind, Coach.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:37.080
Look, I'm not a coach!

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.830
But the way Idiot Ribbon "teaches,"

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:41.500
a hundred years could pass
and you'd still never get better.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:42.250
So-

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:43.290
So?
So-

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:45.370
I'm out!

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:49.000
Huh? You're getting out already?
You have to dry yourself off.

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:54.290
This is Yayoi Takatsuki's "Yayoi-style Radio"!

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:55.580
Um...
This is Yayoi Takatsuki's "Yayoi-style Radio"!

00:08:55.580 --> 00:08:56.250
If you substitute this formula here,
it gets easier to understand.

00:08:56.250 --> 00:09:00.500
If you substitute this formula here,
it gets easier to understand.
Good evening, ya-yoi-yo! I'm Yayoi Takatsuki!

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:01.950
Th-this?

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:05.790
No, not that. You have to enter
the computed value there.

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:07.000
Oh, I see!

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:08.910
Um...

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:12.330
Yukiho?

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:14.120
Yes!

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:19.700
I'm sorry. You really worked hard this
afternoon. It's no wonder you're tired.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:23.750
No, I'm fine. Anyway, this is
no time to be sleeping!

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:26.290
Yeah.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:31.660
Okay! I'm gonna do my best!

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:34.040
Yes. Let's do our best.

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:42.910
How do the girls seem to be doing?

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:48.330
They're working hard,
both of them. Very much so.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:54.540
Haruka is one story, but Yukiho is...

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:56.410
Tough to tell, is it?

00:09:56.450 --> 00:10:01.120
Yes. I hate pinning everything
on this upcoming test,

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:04.330
but in terms of Idolmaster candidacy...

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:08.250
We may have to pull them, huh?

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:12.500
At this point, all we can do is have faith.

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:15.660
In both of them.

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:17.200
Sir.

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:41.080
Ouen shimasu, mainichi ga live!
I'll cheer you on, every day is live!

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:41.870
Haruka Amami
Score: 78
Ouen shimasu, mainichi ga live!
I'll cheer you on, every day is live!

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:42.580
Haruka Amami
Score: 78
Aijou mansai no uta ari, dance ari
There are songs, dances filled with love

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:47.660
Aijou mansai no uta ari, dance ari
There are songs, dances filled with love

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:50.790
Tanoshiku narimashou, bye-bye bad!!
Let's get happy, bye-bye bad!!

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:56.410
Itsudemo mimamotte iru no yo, chikaku de
I'm always watching over you, from up close

00:10:56.410 --> 00:11:00.500
Taisetsu na hito dakara, sou, nandemo shite agetai
Because you're my important person, yes

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:02.540
Taisetsu na hito dakara, sou, nandemo shite agetai
And I want to do everything for you

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:05.410
Koi suru ko, tsuyoi no
Boy I'm in love with, you're so strong

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:08.000
Koi sureba yay yay yay!!
If you're in love, it's yay yay yay!!

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.000
Judgment
Day

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:13.500
Is this really all right?

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:15.870
Moving one of the iDOLs
without permission...

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:18.950
It's all right. I asked Ritsuko to let us.

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:20.500
But...

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:24.330
It's better than suddenly doing it
for real, right? You'll be fine.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:27.540
You've really been working hard.
Have some faith in yourself.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:40.870
Where's Yukiho?

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:44.620
She went back earlier. So, how'd she do?

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:47.370
Mechanically, there were no problems.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:50.790
But, it's the same thing as always.

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:53.540
It's up to Imber, huh?

00:11:55.500 --> 00:12:00.450
Hey, don't tell me... You don't
want to let Yukiho in?

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:05.040
That couldn't be it, right?

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:54.120
Okay, let's go full-speed ahead to the next segment!

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:57.870
I've gotten a TON of postcards recently,
so I'm on cloud nine!

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:00.660
Thanks to all my regular listeners!

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:06.040
Okay, next up is the popular segment
"Special Selection: My Good Luck Charm"!

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:15.540
We'll be back!

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:19.250
It's here for real, huh?

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:20.410
Yes.

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:26.290
To tell the truth, I couldn't sleep at all
last night. How about you?

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:29.450
Yukiho?

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:35.200
Huh? Haruka. When did you...?

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:41.200
Say, would you mind coming
with me for a bit?

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:43.200
Where to?

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:47.290
A little detour!

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:55.330
So, I was listening to
Yayoi's radio show last night,

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:58.290
and you know the tallest building
in the redevelopment district?

00:13:57.080 --> 00:14:00.120
Construction
50m ahead

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:02.250
There's a small O-Inari charm on the roof.

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:07.120
They say that if you pray to it,
your greatest wish will come true.

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:07.120
Urban Restoration and Development Zone

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:09.250
Your greatest wish?

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:09.950
Yup!

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.870
And that's the building!

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:17.120
No
Unauthorized
Access
SAFETY FIRST

00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:20.870
Um, is this all right?
Just barging in like this.

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:23.120
And the time...

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:30.160
We'll be fine! We still have time before the
test. And besides, this is for my dear friend.

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:32.290
Today is special!

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:45.000
This is terrible, huh?

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:48.250
Haruka, I don't think we...

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:57.910
Come on! You too, Yukiho!

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:01.910
Yukiho?

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:09.160
You're amazing, Haruka.

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:15.370
Um, it's a lot sturdier than it looks,
and it's not that wide.

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:18.910
You're someone who,
if you try hard enough,

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:21.790
can come up with an answer. But I...

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:31.250
All I do is get scared. Like, "What if I fail?"
or "What if they don't like me?"

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:36.000
There's no way my greatest wish
can come true.

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:40.120
I can't even be with
the people I hold dearest.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.000
I'll always... be alone.

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:48.540
That's why, even with the Imber...

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:54.250
I used to be that way.

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:59.040
I don't have a father or mother.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:02.290
One day, they just disappeared.

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:07.120
After that, everything was scary.

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:08.200
Like, if I fail, people will hate me.

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:09.370
Haruka! Come on!
Like, if I fail, people will hate me.

00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:11.450
Haruka! Come on!
I'll be alone again.

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:15.290
I couldn't do anything.

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:18.330
Haruka...

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:20.040
But you know what?

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:20.500
You can do it!
But you know what?

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:20.540
You can do it!

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:22.790
You can do it!
Yayoi and the others really supported me.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:24.500
Yayoi and the others really supported me.

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:30.790
And they taught me:

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:32.000
Come on!

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:38.500
If you're scared, your greatest wish
will never come true.

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:51.950
What you need is a strong will and just
a little courage. And you have that, Yukiho.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:57.700
I mean, you've worked so hard!
I'm sure the Imber knows that, too.

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:00.580
It will respond to you.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:04.330
Let's go.

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:26.540
Okay!

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:49.830
Shall we go?

00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:51.080
Yes!

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:04.410
I'm ready.

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:11.700
That's right. I can't be afraid.

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:17.660
I want my greatest wish to come true.

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.080
But why?!

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:31.450
Yukiho is the only one who doesn't pass?

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:36.580
It can't be helped. She couldn't
activate the Imber during her test.

00:18:37.660 --> 00:18:38.660
But...!

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:42.160
I'm sorry, but it's been decided.

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:45.620
It's the same as intercepting the Drops:

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:49.250
There are no do-overs
in what we're trying to do.

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:52.910
Try to understand, Haruka.

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:14.910
My backup?

00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:19.750
Yes. Executing control procedures
from the ground, collating various data...

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:22.910
I'll be supporting you behind the scenes.

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:23.950
But...

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:26.910
The administrator told me.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:28.410
He did?

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:33.950
Miss Amami has potential,
but she's still unreliable.

00:19:34.450 --> 00:19:39.660
That's why I'd like you to
support her. Unfalteringly.

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:45.450
Parakeet
Moving
Center

00:19:45.790 --> 00:19:47.580
It's all right, Haruka.

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:57.080
It's not like I've given up on my greatest
wish. It's just a little different now.

00:19:59.370 --> 00:20:00.580
Haruka.

00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:10.450
I look forward to working
more with you, Haruka.

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:24.330
Let's do our best, both of us.

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:28.500
Let's always be together. Always.

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:35.580
Y-Yukiho?

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:41.370
Hey! You can't sleep out here! Yukiho!

00:20:45.830 --> 00:20:50.370
Iori. Ritsuko. Thank you for everything.

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:54.620
Cut it out. It's not like you have to
thank us for every single thing.

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:55.790
Okay.

00:20:55.790 --> 00:21:00.000
Come on, you don't have to get that
embarrassed, COACH!

00:21:00.370 --> 00:21:01.910
I told you not to call me "Coach"!

00:21:01.910 --> 00:21:02.950
What's this? What're you talking about?
I told you not to call me "Coach"!

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:04.500
What's this? What're you talking about?
Don't be shy, Forehead.

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:05.200
Don't call me "Forehead"!

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:05.830
Coach!
Don't call me "Forehead"!

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:08.040
Shut up, Idiot Ribbon!

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:10.750
Don't call me "Idiot Ribbon," Forehead!

00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:51.540
My greatest wish.

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:54.120
Someday...

00:21:56.160 --> 00:22:05.120
Like a saint that crosses the ages

00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:14.080
In what kind of loneliness did you cry?

00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:22.950
Stretching out to a star so far away

00:22:22.950 --> 00:22:31.500
Say, I'll depict my feelings, look up at the sky

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:42.950
Dear boy, if I always look for you in my heart

00:22:42.950 --> 00:22:51.950
Ah, I'll release a light so strong it will envelop you

00:22:51.950 --> 00:23:00.870
That sparkling trail will be the guide for us both

00:23:00.870 --> 00:23:12.500
Now, no matter where we look, we feel the truth

00:23:25.910 --> 00:23:40.910
Preview
Altitude: 20,000 Meters

00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:27.410
I'm Naze.

00:23:27.410 --> 00:23:27.950
I'm Naraba.

00:23:27.950 --> 00:23:28.870
I'm Sorewa.

00:23:28.870 --> 00:23:30.540
Together, we're Naze...

00:23:30.540 --> 00:23:31.000
Naraba...

00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:31.790
And Sorewa.

00:23:31.790 --> 00:23:34.580
Well, that's about it.
Okay, laughing this time.

00:23:34.580 --> 00:23:35.250
I'm Naze!

00:23:35.250 --> 00:23:36.000
Naraba.

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:36.830
I'm Sorewa!

00:23:36.870 --> 00:23:37.870
And now, crying.

00:23:37.870 --> 00:23:38.540
I'm Naze.

00:23:38.540 --> 00:23:39.120
I'm Naraba.

00:23:39.120 --> 00:23:40.370
I'm Sorewa!
